# Byte-exact checkout on every platform.
#
# MANIFEST.sha256 hashes the exact bytes of each published file. Git's default
# core.autocrlf on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes every hash and
# makes `sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256` fail for reasons that have nothing to do with
# integrity. An integrity manifest that fails on a major platform is worse than no manifest,
# because the reader cannot tell a line-ending conversion from tampering.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, so what you check out is what was hashed.
* -text
